300.−Applicantsfrom18to70yearsoldinclusivearecharged500. Assuming age is processed as an integer number, what is the minimum number of test cases required to achieve 100% coverage for both Equivalence Partitioning and 2-value Boundary Value Analysis?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 3</div><div class="opt correct">c. 6 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 9</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.2 BVA</div><h2>Cau hoi 8</h2><div class="qtext">During the risk identification process, stakeholders analyze various sources to uncover potential product risks, including both known and unknown risks. Which of the following is NOT a direct factor or source used to identify these risks?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Risk management [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Requirement analysis</div><div class="opt ">c. Stakeholder feedback / Interviews</div><div class="opt correct">d. Equivalence Partitions [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 5.2 Nguồn nào ko dc sử dụng để xác định risk thì chọn D vì EP là kỹ thuật thiết kế TC</div><h2>Cau hoi 9</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is an advantage of having the whole team responsible for quality?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Companies no longer need to recruit and train software testing specialists [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Test automation tasks are now the responsibility of the development team instead of the test team</div><div class="opt correct">c. Role barriers are eliminated, and team members contribute to project success based on their unique skills and perspectives [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Project costs are lower because the need for a specialized test team is eliminated</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5.2 whole team approach</div><h2>Cau hoi 10</h2><div class="qtext">Which activities below best represent responsibilities that are consistent with agile development’s Whole Team approach? select TWO</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Testers are responsible for developing unit tests which they pass on to the developers for testing [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">b. Business representatives are expected to select the tools the team will use during the project [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">c. Testers are expected to work with customer representatives to create acceptance tests [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt correct">d. The whole team, not just testers, has responsibility for the quality of the product [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">e. Developers are expected to test non-functional requirements (performance, usability, security, etc.)</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.5.2 về Whole team approach thì định nghĩa là mọi người đều có skill và knowledge để thực hiện any tas, everybody có trách nhiệm về quality, ta chọn C,D</div><h2>Cau hoi 11</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is a benefit of early and frequent feedback?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. The total number of defects found during the project is much higher than on traditional software development projects such as waterfall [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt correct">b. There is less rework because customers see the product regularly [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">c. It is easy to determine the developer who introduces the most defects when integrating code</div><div class="opt ">d. There is enough time to complete all features scheduled for the given iteration</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 3.2.1 Feedback sớm có các lợi ích gì ( chọn less rework)</div><h2>Cau hoi 12</h2><div class="qtext">Which of the following is considered a primary task of a person in a testing role during the test design phase?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. Writing code for automated test fixtures and reviewing developer unit tests. [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. Developing high-level test conditions and setting up the physical test environment.</div><div class="opt correct">c. Designing test cases and designing specific data combinations to support the root cause analysis through proper defect classification. [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. Defining test exit criteria and approving the overall test budget.</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 1.4 Vai trò tester trong Design là C</div><h2>Cau hoi 13</h2><div class="qtext">You are testing software that controls the amount of water sprayed by an automatic sprinkler system, based on the previous 3 days' weather (3 possible conditions: sunny, cloudy, rainy) Maximum water: sunny, sunny, sunny. No water: two or more rainy days. Varying amounts: Other mixes. Question: How many minimum test cases are required to cover all weather combinations according to Equivalence Partitioning criteria?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 3</div><div class="opt correct">c. 21 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 27</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2 nó hỏi các loại hình thời tiết để tính lượng nước tưới cho cây trồng, Input ta có 2 loại input là cá cặp kết hợp thời tiết của 3 ngày và loại cỏ ( cỏ có 5 loại cỏ). Tính kết hợp của thời tiết trong 3 ngày có 3 loại hình S, C, R thì 3*3= 27 TH về thời tiết, nhưng nếu mưa 2 ngày trở lên thì ko tưới nước nên ta gom vào có 7 TH là có 2 ngày mưa trở lên gom về 1 Vậy có 21 TH về thời tiết. Vì kỹ thuật EP nên ta cần 21 TC minimum để test</div><h2>Cau hoi 14</h2><div class="qtext">You review SPEC for a library system: Librarians: 1. Register new borrowers 2. Return books from borrowers 3. Accept fines from borrowers 4. Add new books to the system with their ISBN, author and title 5. Remove books from the system 6. Get system responses within 3 seconds Borrowers : 7. Borrow a maximum of 3 books at one time 8. View the history of books they have borrowed/reserved 9. Be fined for failing to return a book within 3 weeks 10. Get system responses within 3 seconds 11. Borrow a book at no cost for a maximum of 4 weeks 12. Reserve books (if they are on-loan) All users: 13. Can search for books by ISBN, author, or title 14. Can browse the system catalogue 15. The system shall respond to user requests within 3 seconds 16. The user interface shall be easy-to-use Is correct?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 6-10, 6-15, 9-11 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 6-10, 9-11</div><div class="opt correct">c. 6-10, 6-15, 7-12 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 6-15, 7-12</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> refer 3.2.2 review types. Câu này làm rồi trước đây họ hỏi cặp nào mâu thuẫn với nhau nhưng giờ họ sửa đề và hỏi cặp nào là đúng về yêu cầu khi review theo checklist? họ đã sửa đề của ý số 6 trùng với 10, 6 trùng với 15 và thêm nữa 7-12 cũng hợp lý với nhau. Nên câu này chọn các cặp đúng là C</div><h2>Cau hoi 15</h2><div class="qtext">You are going to be testing a small camera. To keep it simple, there are only two buttons: the power button and the shutter button. The camera will act as an automatic focus and exposure camera when the shutter button is pressed halfway and then stopped for 0.4 seconds before the button press is completed. If the shutter button is simply pressed all the way without stop-ping, the camera will act as a single exposure, infinity focus camera. Given the following state transition diagram, how many rows would its matching state transition table contain?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 6 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 10</div><div class="opt ">c. 14</div><div class="opt correct">d. 18 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.2.4 state transition, bài này vẽ bảng state table gồm row là có các trạng thái A, B,C,D, còn cột là các event gồm: Click power button, Press shutter/1st halfway, Press shutter/2nd halfway, Press shutter/ whole way, Done take picture. vẽ ra ta đc bảng có 20 ô ( 4*5) là tương đương 20 TC tuy nhiên AI giải thích là có 2 ô ko xảy ra trong thực tế ( chúng tôi đoán là ở state A ko ấn đc shutter/ 1st và shutter/ 2nd) vì thế đáp án họ chọn 18. cái này cần có kinh nghiệm sử dụng máy ảnh</div><h2>Cau hoi 16</h2><div class="qtext">A decision contains independent atomic conditions. If 100% Modified Condition/Decision Coverage (MC/DC) is achieved using the minimum number of test cases, which of the following statements must be TRUE for each atomic condition? 1. Each atomic condition has been exercised with a TRUE outcome at least once. 2. Each atomic condition has been exercised with a FALSE outcome at least once. 3. Each atomic independently condition has been shown to affect 1 and 2. Which of the following represents the correct set of requirements?</div><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1,2 correct [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 2,3 correct</div><div class="opt ">c. 1,3 correct</div><div class="opt correct">d. 1,2,3 correct [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> Refer 4.3.5 mục định nghĩa của MC/DC</div><h2>Cau hoi 17</h2><div class="qtext">Which of minimum Test case to cover all statements and decision coverage of this code?</div><img src="data:image/png;base64," /><div class="opt selectedwrong">a. 1 [BAN DA CHON - SAI]</div><div class="opt ">b. 2</div><div class="opt correct">c. 3 [DAP AN DUNG]</div><div class="opt ">d. 4</div><div class="explain"><b>Loi giai:</b> </div></body></html>